(
 ']CreateRelease -raw'
 ''
 'Collects everything a GitHub release needs from the Cider project you are working on'
 'and, if there is one, its package config file, and then prints the "gh" command that'
 'would create that release.'
 ''
 '**Nothing is sent to GitHub**: the command is printed for you to check and then run'
 'yourself. Note that "gh" creates the tag as well if it does not exist yet.'
 ''
 'Collected from the Cider config : owner, repository and the distribution folder'
 'Collected from the package config: version, tag and release title'
 'Collected from History          : the release notes for that very version'
 'Collected from the distribution : every file in it, to be selected from'
 ''
 'Whatever could not be collected is reported before the command, so that you know what'
 'to check. A pre-release ("1.0.0-beta-1") takes the notes of its base version ("1.0.0").'
 ''
 'You are asked which of the files in the distribution folder are to be attached to the'
 'release. Selecting none of them is a perfectly good answer. Note that a Tatin package'
 'is not asked about at all: its ZIP file is published on tatin.dev, not on GitHub.'
 ''
 '-raw        Returns the namespace with everything that was collected rather than the'
 '            command, so you can inspect it or amend it and call PrintReleaseCommand.'
)
